// 2026-09-30 초고의 배포된 문장에서 추출했다. kind=web 은 웹 원문의 서술, derived 는 이 문서가 계산하거나 센 것, absence 는 재실행 가능한 검색이 근거다. evidence 는 evidence.jsonl 의 span 을 그대로 옮겼다.
{"id": "c1", "kind": "web", "text": "Sonnet 5.5 에서 thinking: {\"type\": \"disabled\"} 는 400 invalid_request_error 이고 between_tools 로 바꾼다 (02, 05, 06, 16장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Turn off up-front thinking, w1 §Getting started", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1", "quote": "On Claude Sonnet 5.5, `disabled` returns a 400 `invalid_request_error`:"}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking · error", "quote": "\"thinking.type.disabled\" is not supported for this model. Use \"thinking.type.between_tools\" for the lowest thinking setting, or \"thinking.type.adaptive\" and \"output_config.effort\" to control thinking behavior."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1", "quote": "To turn off up-front thinking on Claude Sonnet 5.5, send `thinking: {\"type\": \"between_tools\"}`. It's the lowest thinking setting. Its progress updates between tool calls still come back as `thinking` blocks with their summary text. Without tools, the response contains only text."}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "§Getting started", "quote": "If you run Sonnet with thinking off, you’ll need to switch to the new between_tools setting, which keeps up-front thinking off, before moving to Sonnet 5.5."}]}
{"id": "c2", "kind": "web", "text": "between_tools 는 low, medium, high effort 에서만 받고 xhigh 나 max 에서는 400 이다 (02, 05, 06장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Turn off up-front thinking ¶2", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2", "quote": "`between_tools` works on every platform that offers Claude Sonnet 5.5, with no beta header. It's accepted at `low`, `medium`, and `high` effort. At `xhigh` or `max`, it returns a 400 error."}]}
{"id": "c3", "kind": "web", "text": "between_tools 에 display, budget_tokens, block_binding 을 함께 보내면 400 이고, server-side fallback 으로 Sonnet 5 에 넘어가면 거기서 disabled 로 돈다 (05, 06장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Turn off up-front thinking ¶2", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2", "quote": "`between_tools` takes no other field: `display`, `budget_tokens`, or `block_binding` sent with it returns a 400 error. With [server-side fallback](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#server-side-fallback), a `between_tools` request that falls back to Claude Sonnet 5 runs there with `thinking: {\"type\": \"disabled\"}`."}]}
{"id": "c4", "kind": "web", "text": "between_tools 에서 메시지 단위로 다른 effort 를 보내면 400 이고 턴마다 바꾸려면 adaptive 를 쓴다 (06, 13장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Turn off up-front thinking ¶3", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶3", "quote": "With `between_tools`, effort can't change mid-conversation: a per-message `output_config.effort` that differs from the level in effect returns a 400 error."}]}
{"id": "c5", "kind": "web", "text": "between_tools 는 beta header 없이 모든 플랫폼에서 받고 guide 는 가장 낮은 thinking 설정이라 부르며, tool 없는 요청의 응답은 text 뿐이다 (05, 06장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Turn off up-front thinking", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2", "quote": "`between_tools` works on every platform that offers Claude Sonnet 5.5, with no beta header. It's accepted at `low`, `medium`, and `high` effort. At `xhigh` or `max`, it returns a 400 error."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1", "quote": "To turn off up-front thinking on Claude Sonnet 5.5, send `thinking: {\"type\": \"between_tools\"}`. It's the lowest thinking setting. Its progress updates between tool calls still come back as `thinking` blocks with their summary text. Without tools, the response contains only text."}]}
{"id": "c6", "kind": "web", "text": "guide 의 Before 예시는 disabled 와 xhigh 이고 After 예시는 between_tools 와 high 다 (05장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Turn off up-front thinking 예시", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking · Before example", "quote": "      thinking={\"type\": \"disabled\"},\n      output_config={\"effort\": \"xhigh\"},"}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking · After example", "quote": "      thinking={\"type\": \"between_tools\"},\n      output_config={\"effort\": \"high\"},"}]}
{"id": "c7", "kind": "web", "text": "xhigh 를 지키려면 thinking 필드를 빼거나 adaptive 로 돌린다 (05장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Turn off up-front thinking ¶2", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2", "quote": "To run at those levels, use adaptive thinking: omit the `thinking` field or send `thinking: {\"type\": \"adaptive\"}`."}]}
{"id": "c8", "kind": "web", "text": "tool_choice 의 any 와 tool 은 token counting endpoint 까지 400 이고 auto 와 none 은 받는다 (02, 07장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Forced tool use, d4 §Forced tool use", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Forced tool use", "quote": "Every earlier model on this page accepts a `tool_choice` of type `any` or `tool`. Claude Sonnet 5.5 rejects both with a 400 error, including on the [token counting](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/token-counting) endpoint:"}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Forced tool use is not supported", "quote": "`tool_choice: {\"type\": \"auto\"}` (the default) and `{\"type\": \"none\"}` are supported. The same check applies to the [token counting](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/token-counting) endpoint."}]}
{"id": "c9", "kind": "web", "text": "대안은 auto 와 strict: true 이고 모델이 tool 없이 답할 수 있으므로 호출 조건을 프롬프트에 적으며, strict 는 모든 object 에 additionalProperties: false 가 필요하다 (07장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Forced tool use ¶2", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Forced tool use ¶2", "quote": "Send `tool_choice: {\"type\": \"auto\"}`, and mark the tool `strict: true` so its input matches the schema. The model can then answer without calling the tool, so say in the prompt when to use it."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Forced tool use ¶2", "quote": "[Strict tool use](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/strict-tool-use) supports a subset of JSON Schema and needs `additionalProperties: false` on every object."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Forced tool use · After example", "quote": "\"content\": \"What'\\''s the weather in Paris? Use the get_weather tool.\""}]}
{"id": "c10", "kind": "web", "text": "strict tool 은 요청당 20개까지이고 MCP, computer use, browser use toolset 에는 strict 를 붙일 수 없다 (07장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Forced tool use ¶3", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Forced tool use ¶3", "quote": "A request can have at most 20 strict tools, and the MCP, computer use, and browser use toolset entries don't accept `strict`."}]}
{"id": "c11", "kind": "web", "text": "Amazon Bedrock 에서는 structured outputs 를 못 쓰므로 strict 없이 auto 를 보내고 입력을 코드에서 검증한다 (07장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Forced tool use ¶2", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Forced tool use ¶2", "quote": "On Amazon Bedrock, [structured outputs](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/structured-outputs), which include strict tool use, aren't available for Claude Sonnet 5.5. There, send `auto` without `strict`, say in the prompt when to call the tool, and validate the tool input in your code."}]}
{"id": "c12", "kind": "web", "text": "블록 앞의 system, tools, 이전 메시지를 고치고 블록을 다시 보내면 Claude API, Bedrock, Google Cloud 에서 2026-08-31 00:00 UTC 이후 만든 계정에 기본으로 400 이다 (02, 04, 08장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d4 §Thinking blocks are tied, d1 §Thinking blocks are tied ¶2", "evidence": [{"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "The API also checks whether anything before a Claude Sonnet 5.5 thinking block has changed since the block was produced: the `system` prompt, the `tools`, or an earlier message."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied ¶2", "quote": "For accounts created on or after August 31, 2026, 00:00 UTC, the API enforces this by default, on the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, and Google Cloud. On those accounts, a request that replays a block after an edit to earlier history returns a 400 error."}]}
{"id": "c13", "kind": "web", "text": "drop_block 은 thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01 beta header 가 필요하고 adaptive 에서만 되며, between_tools 는 고친 턴부터 블록을 떼고, 이전 계정은 이 필드를 보내면 검사에 들어간다 (08장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d4 §Thinking blocks are tied", "evidence": [{"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "To drop the affected blocks instead, send the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header and set `thinking.block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior` to `\"drop_block\"`. On older accounts, setting that field to either value opts the request in. `block_binding` works only with `thinking: {\"type\": \"adaptive\"}`."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "With `between_tools`, keep the history append-only, or strip the thinking blocks from the edited turn on."}]}
{"id": "c14", "kind": "web", "text": "이전 계정은 검사가 기본으로 꺼져 있어 오래된 계정에서 통과하던 코드가 새 계정에서 처음 400 을 낼 수 있다 (04장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Thinking blocks are tied ¶2, d4", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied ¶2", "quote": "For accounts created on or after August 31, 2026, 00:00 UTC, the API enforces this by default, on the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, and Google Cloud. On those accounts, a request that replays a block after an edit to earlier history returns a 400 error."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "To drop the affected blocks instead, send the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header and set `thinking.block_binding.prefix_mismatch_behavior` to `\"drop_block\"`. On older accounts, setting that field to either value opts the request in. `block_binding` works only with `thinking: {\"type\": \"adaptive\"}`."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "With `between_tools`, keep the history append-only, or strip the thinking blocks from the edited turn on."}], "note": "앞 문장은 'on or after August 31' 계정에만 기본 적용이라는 guide 문장과 이전 계정은 opt-in 이라는 What's new 문장에서 끌어낸 추론"}
{"id": "c15", "kind": "web", "text": "Sonnet 5.5 블록은 만든 계정이나 연결된 계정에서만 쓰이고 다른 계정이 보내면 블록이 빠진 채 200 이다 (08장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Thinking blocks are tied ¶2, d4 §Thinking blocks stay with the account", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied ¶2", "quote": "Thinking blocks that Claude Sonnet 5.5 produces work only in the account that produced them, or in an account linked to it."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks stay with the account that produced them", "quote": "When another account sends one of these blocks, the API drops the block before the model sees it, and the request succeeds."}]}
{"id": "c16", "kind": "web", "text": "Sonnet 5.5 는 Sonnet 5 블록을 읽고 Opus 5, Opus 5.5 블록은 읽지 않으며, 빠진 블록은 200 이고 과금되지 않으며 beta header 를 보내면 input_transformations 에 보고된다 (03, 08장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Thinking blocks are tied ¶1, d4", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied ¶1", "quote": "Claude Sonnet 5.5 reads thinking blocks from Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Haiku 4.5, and earlier models. It doesn't read blocks from Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, or any Claude Fable or Claude Mythos model. The API drops blocks the model can't read. The request still returns 200, and dropped blocks aren't billed."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "With the `thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01` beta header, the drop is reported in a top-level `input_transformations` array."}]}
{"id": "c17", "kind": "web", "text": "Sonnet 5.5 블록은 어느 모델도 읽지 않아서 다른 모델로 넘어간 대화는 그 뒤 reasoning 없이 돈다 (08장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d4 §Thinking blocks are tied", "evidence": [{"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied ¶1", "quote": "No other model reads Claude Sonnet 5.5 thinking blocks."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied", "quote": "So a conversation that moves from Claude Sonnet 5 onto Claude Sonnet 5.5 keeps its reasoning, and one that moves from Claude Sonnet 5.5 to any other model runs the turns after the switch without it."}]}
{"id": "c18", "kind": "web", "text": "Claude API 와 Google Cloud 에서 computer_20251124 는 400 이고 computer_toolset_20260801 만 받으며 Bedrock 에서는 computer_20251124 를 보낸다 (02, 09장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Computer use", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Computer use", "quote": "On the Claude API and Google Cloud, Claude Sonnet 5.5 supports computer use only through the `computer_toolset_20260801` toolset. There, `computer_20251124` returns a 400 error. Claude Sonnet 5.5 doesn't accept `computer_20250124` on any platform."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Computer use · table", "quote": "| `computer_20251124`    | Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Sonnet 4.6                   | `computer_toolset_20260801`             | `computer_20251124`    |"}]}
{"id": "c19", "kind": "web", "text": "toolset 옆의 fine-grained-tool-streaming-2025-05-14 beta header 는 400 이고 tool 마다 eager_input_streaming 을 쓴다 (09장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Computer use ¶2", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Computer use ¶2", "quote": "If you send the `fine-grained-tool-streaming-2025-05-14` beta header, remove it when you move to the toolset. Alongside a toolset entry, it returns a 400 error. Set `eager_input_streaming: true` on each tool that needs it instead."}]}
{"id": "c20", "kind": "web", "text": "advisor tool 은 beta 이고 Sonnet 5.5 executor 는 Opus 5, Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5, Fable 5, 5.1, Mythos 5, 5.1 advisor 를 받으며 Sonnet 5, Sonnet 4.6, Opus 4.6~4.8 은 400 이고 조언은 advisor_redacted_result 로 암호화된다 (02, 09장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Advisor tool, d4", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Advisor tool", "quote": "With the [advisor tool](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/advisor-tool), a Claude Sonnet 5.5 executor needs one of these advisors: Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Fable 5, Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5, or Claude Mythos 5.1."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Advisor tool", "quote": "Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 5, and Claude Sonnet 4.6 advisors return a 400 error. The advice comes back encrypted as an `advisor_redacted_result` block, so its text isn't readable in the response."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Some advisor tool pairings are not supported", "quote": "With the [advisor tool](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/advisor-tool) (beta), a Claude Sonnet 5.5 executor needs Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5, Claude Fable 5, Claude Opus 5.5, or Claude Opus 5 as its advisor, or Claude Sonnet 5.5 itself."}]}
{"id": "c21", "kind": "web", "text": "toolset 은 member tool_use 블록, batch action, toolset_name 을 써서 agent loop 도 바뀌고, 이미 toolset 을 보내는 코드와 browser use tool 은 바꿀 것이 없다 (09장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d4 §computer_20251124, d1 §Computer use ¶3", "evidence": [{"source": "d4", "locator": "§computer_20251124 is not supported", "quote": "Drop the beta header, replace the `tools` entry with `{\"type\": \"computer_toolset_20260801\"}`, and update your agent loop for member `tool_use` blocks, batch actions, and `toolset_name` on results."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Computer use ¶3", "quote": "Code that already sends the toolset needs no change. [Migrate from `computer_20251124`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/computer-use-tool#migrate-from-computer-20251124) lists the request and agent-loop changes."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§computer_20251124 is not supported", "quote": "Integrations that already use the toolset, and the [browser use tool](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/browser-use-tool), need no change."}]}
{"id": "c22", "kind": "web", "text": "tool call 사이의 한두 문장보다 긴 메모는 기본 display 에서 빈 progress thinking 블록으로 오고 짧은 말은 text 로 남으며, Sonnet 5 는 모두 text 였고 요청은 실패하지 않지만 화면이 멈춘다 (02, 03, 10장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Text between tool calls ¶1", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Text between tool calls ¶1", "quote": "On Claude Sonnet 5.5, notes longer than a sentence or two that the model writes between tool calls come back as [progress-update `thinking` blocks](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/thinking#progress-updates), empty at the default `display`. Shorter remarks stay `text`."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Text between tool calls ¶1", "quote": "On Claude Sonnet 5 and earlier models, all text between tool calls comes back as `text` blocks. No request fails, but an interface that shows those notes goes quiet."}]}
{"id": "c23", "kind": "web", "text": "display 를 updates(beta header) 나 summarized 로 두고 비어 있지 않은 thinking 블록을 뒤따르는 tool_use 앞에 그리며, between_tools 는 display 없이 요약 텍스트가 든 thinking 블록으로 온다 (06, 10, 16장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Text between tool calls ¶2, §Turn off up-front thinking", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Text between tool calls ¶2", "quote": "With adaptive thinking, set `display` to `\"updates\"` (beta, `thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18` header) to get the updates alone, or to `\"summarized\"` to get them mixed with reasoning. Render each non-empty `thinking` block before the `tool_use` block that follows it."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Text between tool calls ¶2", "quote": "With [`between_tools`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/migration-guide#turn-off-up-front-thinking), the text comes back without `display`."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1", "quote": "To turn off up-front thinking on Claude Sonnet 5.5, send `thinking: {\"type\": \"between_tools\"}`. It's the lowest thinking setting. Its progress updates between tool calls still come back as `thinking` blocks with their summary text. Without tools, the response contains only text."}]}
{"id": "c24", "kind": "web", "text": "between_tools 에서 progress 블록을 그대로 되돌려 보내면 모델은 요약이 아니라 자기가 쓴 메모 전체를 받는다 (10장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d4 §Turn off up-front thinking with between_tools", "evidence": [{"source": "d4", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking with between_tools", "quote": "Pass those blocks back unchanged with the rest of the assistant turn. A progress-update block you send back gives the model the full note it wrote, not the summary."}]}
{"id": "c25", "kind": "web", "text": "Sonnet 5.5 는 Sonnet 5 보다 많은 부류에서 거절하고 stop_details 부류는 cyber, bio, frontier_llm, reasoning_extraction, general_harms 다섯이며 general_harms 는 무해한 일도 걸릴 수 있다 (02, 11장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Safety classifiers and fallback", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Safety classifiers and fallback", "quote": "Claude Sonnet 5.5 declines in more categories than Claude Sonnet 5. A decline returns `stop_reason: \"refusal\"`, and its `stop_details` can name one of these [categories](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#refusal-response):"}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Safety classifiers and fallback", "quote": "* **`\"general_harms\"`:** The request falls under another usage-policy area. Benign work can also trigger this category."}]}
{"id": "c26", "kind": "web", "text": "거부는 HTTP 200 에 stop_reason refusal 로 온다 (02, 03, 11장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d4 §Refusals, fallback, and billing", "evidence": [{"source": "d4", "locator": "§Refusals, fallback, and billing", "quote": "A declined request returns HTTP 200 with `stop_reason: \"refusal\"` and a [`stop_details`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#refusal-response) object naming the policy area."}]}
{"id": "c27", "kind": "web", "text": "server-side fallback(fallbacks: default, beta, Claude API 만)은 cyber 와 frontier_llm 만 Sonnet 5 로 재시도하고 bio, reasoning_extraction, general_harms 는 재시도하지 않는다. between_tools 요청이 넘어가면 disabled 로 돈다 (05, 11장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Safety classifiers and fallback ¶2", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Safety classifiers and fallback ¶2", "quote": "[Server-side fallback](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#server-side-fallback) (`fallbacks: \"default\"`, beta, Claude API only) retries `\"cyber\"` and `\"frontier_llm\"` declines on Claude Sonnet 5. It doesn't retry `\"bio\"`, `\"reasoning_extraction\"`, or `\"general_harms\"` declines."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶2", "quote": "`between_tools` takes no other field: `display`, `budget_tokens`, or `block_binding` sent with it returns a 400 error. With [server-side fallback](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/refusals-and-fallback#server-side-fallback), a `between_tools` request that falls back to Claude Sonnet 5 runs there with `thinking: {\"type\": \"disabled\"}`."}]}
{"id": "c28", "kind": "web", "text": "소개 글은 일상적인 버그 수정은 그대로 되고 위험도가 높은 보안 작업은 눈에 보이게 Sonnet 5 로 넘어간다고 적고, bio 오탐을 인정한다 (11장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §Safety · Safeguards", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Safeguards · Cybersecurity", "quote": "Users can still find and fix bugs in their code as part of routine software development, but higher-risk cybersecurity tasks will visibly fall back to Sonnet 5."}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "§Safety · Safeguards · Biology", "quote": "These target harmful requests; most research, education, and clinical work is unaffected, though some microbiology and virology requests may be flagged in error."}]}
{"id": "c29", "kind": "web", "text": "거부가 과금되는지는 부류에 따라 다르다 (11장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d4 §Refusals, fallback, and billing", "evidence": [{"source": "d4", "locator": "§Refusals, fallback, and billing", "quote": "Whether a refusal that arrives before any output is billed depends on its refusal category, and it counts against your rate limits either way."}]}
{"id": "c30", "kind": "web", "text": "소개 글은 Sonnet 5 보다 30% 넘게 빠르고 대부분의 작업에서 최대 30% 싸다고 쓴다 (03장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §intro", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§intro ¶1", "quote": "Introducing Claude Sonnet 5.5, the second model in the Claude 5.5 family. It’s a clear upgrade over Claude Sonnet 5, runs 30%+ faster, and costs up to 30% less for most work."}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "§intro · Speed", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 generates outputs 30%+ faster than Sonnet 5, making it our fastest Sonnet model to date."}]}
{"id": "c31", "kind": "web", "text": "가격은 입력 100만 토큰당 $2, 출력 $10, cache read $0.20 으로 Sonnet 5 와 같고 절감은 토큰 수에서 온다 (02, 03장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §intro · Cost, d1 §intro", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§intro · Cost", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 is priced the same as Sonnet 5 at $2 per million input tokens, $10 per million output tokens, and $0.20 per million tokens for cache reads, but it typically needs far fewer tokens to do the same work. In our testing, it costs up to 30% less per task than its predecessor."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§intro ¶2", "quote": "Claude Sonnet 5.5 has the same prices as Claude Sonnet 5."}]}
{"id": "c32", "kind": "derived", "text": "Sonnet 5 최고점을 처음 넘는 Sonnet 5.5 단계의 비용 비는 Terminal-Bench 1/15(low), FrontierCode 1/24(high), CursorBench 1/14(low), AA-Briefcase 1/9(medium) 이다 (12장, meta summary)", "verdict": "derived", "scope": "w1 차트 점에서 계산", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "chart Terminal-Bench 4.0", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 20.0% $0.76 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 28.8% $0.83 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 43.0% $1.94 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 61.5% $5.30 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 70.6% $12.54"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart Terminal-Bench 4.0", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 4.5% $8.20 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 10.3% $11.62"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart Terminal-Bench 4.0", "quote": "Opus 5.5 · Xhigh: 66.4% $7.35 / Opus 5.5 · Max: 64.8% $11.24 / Sonnet 5 · Low: 3.2% $3.78 / Sonnet 5 · Med: 4.4% $4.83 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 7.0% $9.95 / GPT-5.6 Sol · Low: 7.9% $1.46 / GPT-5.6 Sol · Max: 37.3% $7.89"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart FrontierCode v1.1 main", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 29.3% $0.19 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 36.5% $0.24 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 49.4% $0.42 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 52.1% $1.59 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 46.2% $20.78"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart FrontierCode v1.1 main", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 39.4% $6.10 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 42.7% $10.07 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 42.4% $17.12 / GPT-6 Sol · Max: 49.3% $2.07"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart CursorBench 4.0", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 35.8% $0.50 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 39.2% $0.70 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 47.8% $1.67 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 53.1% $3.88 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 55.5% $9.67"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart CursorBench 4.0", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 30.8% $3.48 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 34.1% $7.17"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart AA-Briefcase v1.1", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 1264.0 $0.87 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 1461.0 $1.64 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 1634.0 $3.95 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 1746.0 $9.63 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 1811.0 $29.19"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart AA-Briefcase v1.1", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 1177.0 $3.76 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 1359.0 $14.43 / Opus 5.5 · Max: 1822.0 $21.05"}], "note": "원문은 이 비교를 하지 않는다. 0.76/11.62=0.065, 0.42/10.07=0.042, 0.50/7.17=0.070, 1.64/14.43=0.114", "derived_from": ["0.76", "11.62", "0.42", "10.07", "0.50", "7.17", "1.64", "14.43"]}
{"id": "c33", "kind": "derived", "text": "Sonnet 5.5 max 비용은 네 벤치마크 모두 Sonnet 5 max 보다 높다: $12.54/$11.62, $20.78/$17.12, $9.67/$7.17, $29.19/$14.43 (02, 12장)", "verdict": "derived", "scope": "w1 차트 점에서 계산", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "chart Terminal-Bench 4.0", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 20.0% $0.76 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 28.8% $0.83 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 43.0% $1.94 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 61.5% $5.30 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 70.6% $12.54"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart Terminal-Bench 4.0", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 4.5% $8.20 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 10.3% $11.62"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart Terminal-Bench 4.0", "quote": "Opus 5.5 · Xhigh: 66.4% $7.35 / Opus 5.5 · Max: 64.8% $11.24 / Sonnet 5 · Low: 3.2% $3.78 / Sonnet 5 · Med: 4.4% $4.83 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 7.0% $9.95 / GPT-5.6 Sol · Low: 7.9% $1.46 / GPT-5.6 Sol · Max: 37.3% $7.89"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart FrontierCode v1.1 main", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 29.3% $0.19 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 36.5% $0.24 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 49.4% $0.42 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 52.1% $1.59 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 46.2% $20.78"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart FrontierCode v1.1 main", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 39.4% $6.10 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 42.7% $10.07 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 42.4% $17.12 / GPT-6 Sol · Max: 49.3% $2.07"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart CursorBench 4.0", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 35.8% $0.50 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 39.2% $0.70 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 47.8% $1.67 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 53.1% $3.88 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 55.5% $9.67"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart CursorBench 4.0", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 30.8% $3.48 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 34.1% $7.17"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart AA-Briefcase v1.1", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 1264.0 $0.87 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 1461.0 $1.64 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 1634.0 $3.95 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 1746.0 $9.63 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 1811.0 $29.19"}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "chart AA-Briefcase v1.1", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 1177.0 $3.76 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 1359.0 $14.43 / Opus 5.5 · Max: 1822.0 $21.05"}], "note": "원문은 max 끼리 비교하지 않는다. 1.08, 1.21, 1.35, 2.02 배", "derived_from": ["12.54", "11.62", "20.78", "17.12", "9.67", "7.17", "29.19", "14.43"]}
{"id": "c34", "kind": "derived", "text": "FrontierCode 에서 Sonnet 5.5 max 는 46.2% 로 xhigh 52.1% 보다 낮고 비용은 13배다 (12장)", "verdict": "derived", "scope": "w1 FrontierCode 차트에서 계산", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "chart FrontierCode v1.1 main", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 · Low: 29.3% $0.19 / Sonnet 5.5 · Med: 36.5% $0.24 / Sonnet 5.5 · High: 49.4% $0.42 / Sonnet 5.5 · Xhigh: 52.1% $1.59 / Sonnet 5.5 · Max: 46.2% $20.78"}], "note": "20.78/1.59=13.07", "derived_from": ["20.78", "1.59"]}
{"id": "c35", "kind": "web", "text": "FrontierCode 에서 Sonnet 5 는 xhigh 42.7% 가 max 42.4% 보다 높다 (12장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 FrontierCode 차트", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "chart FrontierCode v1.1 main", "quote": "Sonnet 5 · High: 39.4% $6.10 / Sonnet 5 · Xhigh: 42.7% $10.07 / Sonnet 5 · Max: 42.4% $17.12 / GPT-6 Sol · Max: 49.3% $2.07"}]}
{"id": "c36", "kind": "web", "text": "소개 글은 낮은 effort 의 Sonnet 5.5 가 여러 벤치마크에서 Sonnet 5 최고점을 약 1/10 비용으로 넘는다고 쓴다 (12장 첨언)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §Performance · charts", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance · charts ¶", "quote": "On several benchmarks, Sonnet 5.5 at Low or Medium effort beats Sonnet 5’s best score for about a tenth of the cost per task. It complements Opus 5.5 best when running at lower effort settings, where it costs less per task. At higher settings, it can perform comparably at a similar cost."}]}
{"id": "c37", "kind": "web", "text": "각주 2 는 FrontierCode max 역전을 Claude Code code-review skill 이 subagent 로 나눠 돈 탓의 timeout 과 범위 밖 수정으로 설명한다 (12, 15장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §Footnotes 2", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Footnotes 2", "quote": "Sonnet 5.5 scores lower at Max effort than at Xhigh. FrontierCode evaluates whether a code change could be merged without human edits. It penalizes out-of-scope changes, even if they are high-quality or helpful."}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "§Footnotes 2", "quote": "At Max effort, Sonnet 5.5 more often ran Claude Code’s code-review skill, which splits the review across many subagents, and in two cases Cognition examined, this led to a timeout or to extra edits beyond the task’s scope, and therefore to a lower score."}]}
{"id": "c38", "kind": "web", "text": "GDPval-AA 와 AA-Briefcase 는 structured outputs 버그가 있던 출시 전 배포에서 쟀고 원문은 영향이 작고 점수를 낮춰 잡는 쪽이라 본다 (12, 15장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §Footnotes 3, 4", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Footnotes 3", "quote": "Artificial Analysis ran GDPval-AA and AA-Briefcase on a pre-release deployment of Sonnet 5.5 on the Claude Platform, which we found to have a bug that could degrade responses to requests that use structured outputs."}, {"source": "w1", "locator": "§Footnotes 3", "quote": "We expect the effect on Sonnet 5.5’s scores, if any, to be small and to understate its performance."}]}
{"id": "c39", "kind": "web", "text": "소개 글은 복잡하고 열린 작업에서 Opus 5.5 가 여전히 낫다고 스스로 적는다 (15장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §Performance ¶1", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Performance ¶1", "quote": "On several evaluations, Sonnet 5.5 at Max effort even performs comparably to Opus 5.5. However, benchmark scores capture only one facet of a model’s capabilities; in our own testing, and in that of external testers, Opus 5.5 remains clearly stronger at complex, open-ended work requiring sustained judgment."}]}
{"id": "c40", "kind": "web", "text": "effort 단계는 다시 맞춰져 같은 단계가 Sonnet 5 와 같은 양의 thinking 을 내지 않고, Claude API 기본은 high 다 (02, 13장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Recommended changes, d3", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Recommended changes", "quote": "Re-run your effort sweep. Claude Sonnet 5.5 has five effort levels: `low`, `medium`, `high`, `xhigh`, and `max`. The default on the Claude API is `high`. The levels are recalibrated, so a level doesn't produce the same amount of thinking as on Claude Sonnet 5."}, {"source": "d3", "locator": "§Recommended effort levels for Claude Sonnet 5", "quote": "Claude Sonnet 5 defaults to `high` effort on the Claude API and Claude Code."}]}
{"id": "c41", "kind": "web", "text": "시작 effort 는 agentic coding 과 여러 단계 tool 사용은 medium, 더 길거나 어려우면 high, 채팅은 medium 이나 low, 그 밖은 high 이고 xhigh 와 max 는 eval 이 품질 이득을 보일 때만 쓴다 (13장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Recommended changes, d3 §Sonnet 5.5", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Recommended changes", "quote": "Start at `high` unless your workload is agentic or latency-sensitive. For agentic coding and multistep tool use, start at `medium` for well-specified tasks and move to `high` for harder or longer ones. For chat and other latency-sensitive work, start at `medium` or `low`."}, {"source": "d3", "locator": "§Recommended effort levels for Claude Sonnet 5.5", "quote": "Use `xhigh` or `max` only where your evals show a quality gain. Set `max_tokens` with room for thinking and the reply."}]}
{"id": "c42", "kind": "web", "text": "Claude Code 기본 effort 는 Sonnet 5 의 high 에서 Sonnet 5.5 의 medium 으로 바뀐다 (13장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "w1 §Cost and speed ¶2, d3 §Sonnet 5", "evidence": [{"source": "w1", "locator": "§Cost and speed ¶2", "quote": "In Claude Code and our apps, the default effort is set to Medium, while the Claude Platform defaults to High."}, {"source": "d3", "locator": "§Recommended effort levels for Claude Sonnet 5", "quote": "Claude Sonnet 5 defaults to `high` effort on the Claude API and Claude Code."}], "note": "두 출처를 맞대어 본 것. 소개 글은 Claude Code 와 앱의 기본을 Medium 이라 적는다"}
{"id": "c43", "kind": "web", "text": "top-level effort 를 바꾸면 cache breakpoint 가 깨지고, Sonnet 5.5 는 메시지 단위 effort(beta header) 로 캐시를 지키며 이 기능은 Sonnet 5 에 없다 (13장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d2 §Prompt caching, d3, d4 §Feature support", "evidence": [{"source": "d2", "locator": "§Prompt caching", "quote": "The resolved effort value is rendered into the prompt, so changing it between requests invalidates cache breakpoints, just as changing the legacy [`budget_tokens`](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/extended-thinking#extended-thinking-with-prompt-caching) parameter does on models that use it."}, {"source": "d2", "locator": "§Prompt caching", "quote": "Setting `effort` explicitly to the model's default is equivalent to omitting it and does not break the cache."}, {"source": "d3", "locator": "§Change effort mid-conversation", "quote": "On Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5.1, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Opus 5, and Claude Sonnet 5.5, use a per-message effort change, which keeps the prompt cache. On other models, set a new top-level value on the next request, which starts the cache over."}, {"source": "d3", "locator": "§Per-message effort (beta)", "quote": "Per-message effort is in beta and requires the [beta header](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/api/beta-headers) `mid-conversation-output-config-2026-07-01`."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Feature support", "quote": "Per-message effort, mid-conversation system messages, and mid-conversation tool changes aren't available on Claude Sonnet 5, whose minimum cacheable prompt is 1,024 tokens."}]}
{"id": "c44", "kind": "web", "text": "캐시할 수 있는 최소 프롬프트가 1,024 토큰에서 512 토큰으로 줄었다 (13장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Other changes", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Other changes", "quote": "* **Prompt caching:** The minimum cacheable prompt is 512 tokens, down from 1,024 on Claude Sonnet 5, Claude Sonnet 4.6, and Claude Sonnet 4.5."}]}
{"id": "c45", "kind": "web", "text": "max_tokens 는 thinking 과 답을 합친 요청 하나의 상한이고 agentic coding 은 128,000 과 streaming 을 권하며, tool-use loop 에서는 요청마다 따로 걸린다 (13장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Handle thinking, d3, d2 §Cost control", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Handle thinking in responses", "quote": "* **Revisit `max_tokens`.** It covers thinking plus text, and thinking tokens are billed as output tokens."}, {"source": "d3", "locator": "§Recommended effort levels for Claude Sonnet 5.5", "quote": "For agentic coding, set `max_tokens` to 128,000, the model's maximum, and [stream](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/streaming) the response."}, {"source": "d2", "locator": "§Cost control", "quote": "In a tool-use loop, each request in the turn has its own `max_tokens`, so it doesn't bound the whole turn's spend."}]}
{"id": "c46", "kind": "web", "text": "모델 ID 는 날짜 접미사 없는 claude-sonnet-5-5 이고 Bedrock 은 anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5 다 (05, 16장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Migrating from Sonnet 5 ¶1, d4 §Availability", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Migrating from Sonnet 5 ¶1", "quote": "Replace your model ID with `claude-sonnet-5-5`, which has no date suffix."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Migrating from Sonnet 5 ¶1", "quote": "On other platforms, use the ID listed under [Availability](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/sonnet-5-5/whats-new-sonnet-5-5#availability)."}, {"source": "d4", "locator": "§Availability", "quote": "* **AWS:** [Claude in Amazon Bedrock](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/claude-in-amazon-bedrock), as `anthropic.claude-sonnet-5-5`, and [Claude Platform on AWS](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/claude-platform-on-aws), as `claude-sonnet-5-5`."}]}
{"id": "c47", "kind": "web", "text": "Claude Managed Agents 는 모델 이름 외에 바꿀 것이 없다 (04장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §intro note", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§intro note", "quote": "If you use [Claude Managed Agents](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/managed-agents/overview), no changes beyond updating the model name are required."}]}
{"id": "c48", "kind": "web", "text": "/claude-api migrate 는 모델 ID 교체, 깨지는 파라미터, effort 조정을 코드 전반에 적용하고 확인 목록을 만든다 (16장)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §intro tip", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§intro tip", "quote": "The skill applies the model ID swap and, as needed, breaking parameter changes, prefill replacement, and effort calibration for your target model across your code base, then produces a checklist of items to verify manually."}]}
{"id": "c49", "kind": "web", "text": "guide 는 Sonnet 5 코드가 블록을 type 으로 읽고 되돌려 보내는 두 항목을 이미 갖췄다고 보고 thinking 없이 돌던 코드는 세 항목 모두 필요하다고 적는다 (02장 첨언)", "verdict": "confirmed", "scope": "d1 §Handle thinking in responses", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Handle thinking in responses", "quote": "Code that ran without thinking needs all three items. Code from Claude Sonnet 5 likely has the first two."}]}
{"id": "c50", "kind": "derived", "text": "Sonnet 5 코드에서 400 을 받는 설정은 다섯 종류다: disabled, forced tool_choice, 고친 기록의 블록 재전송, computer_20251124, 받지 않는 advisor (02, 16장, meta summary)", "verdict": "derived", "scope": "d1 Sonnet 5 절을 세어 정리", "evidence": [{"source": "d1", "locator": "§Turn off up-front thinking ¶1", "quote": "On Claude Sonnet 5.5, `disabled` returns a 400 `invalid_request_error`:"}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Forced tool use", "quote": "Every earlier model on this page accepts a `tool_choice` of type `any` or `tool`. Claude Sonnet 5.5 rejects both with a 400 error, including on the [token counting](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-with-claude/token-counting) endpoint:"}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Thinking blocks are tied ¶2", "quote": "For accounts created on or after August 31, 2026, 00:00 UTC, the API enforces this by default, on the Claude API, Amazon Bedrock, and Google Cloud. On those accounts, a request that replays a block after an edit to earlier history returns a 400 error."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Computer use", "quote": "On the Claude API and Google Cloud, Claude Sonnet 5.5 supports computer use only through the `computer_toolset_20260801` toolset. There, `computer_20251124` returns a 400 error. Claude Sonnet 5.5 doesn't accept `computer_20250124` on any platform."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Advisor tool", "quote": "With the [advisor tool](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/agents-and-tools/tool-use/advisor-tool), a Claude Sonnet 5.5 executor needs one of these advisors: Claude Opus 5, Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Sonnet 5.5, Claude Fable 5, Claude Fable 5.1, Claude Mythos 5, or Claude Mythos 5.1."}, {"source": "d1", "locator": "§Advisor tool", "quote": "Claude Opus 4.8, Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Opus 4.6, Claude Sonnet 5, and Claude Sonnet 4.6 advisors return a 400 error. The advice comes back encrypted as an `advisor_redacted_result` block, so its text isn't readable in the response."}], "note": "guide 는 개수를 적지 않는다. between_tools 의 부수 조건과 beta header 400 은 다섯 종류 안의 하위 조건으로 셌다", "derived_from": ["disabled", "tool_choice", "prefix", "computer_20251124", "advisor"]}
